<title>UK: Tate &amp; Lyle down after NatWest comment. [CORRECTED 09:44 GMT]</title>
<headline>Tate &amp; Lyle down after NatWest comment. [CORRECTED 09:44 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Tate &amp; Lyle Plc dropped on Wednesday after analysts at NatWest Securities downgraded the stock amid worries about the impact on profits of downward pressure on high fructose syrup prices (corrects from &quot;rising fructose syrup prices&quot;), dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock was down 13p at 454 by 0850 GMT in volume of 669,723 shares.  </p>
<p>No-one at NatWest was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
